  "faq_title": "Frequently asked questions",
  "faq_q1": "Does it work with MT4/MT5?",
  "faq_a1": "Yes. Export your history from MetaTrader (CSV or Excel .xlsx file) and import it in 2 clicks. TradeDiscipline automatically recognises MT4/MT5 formats and most brokers.",
  "faq_q2": "Can I use it without a prop firm?",
  "faq_a2": "Absolutely. TradeDiscipline works for all types of traders: personal account, prop firm, or both. Prop firm challenge tracking is optional.",
  "faq_q3": "What exactly does the AI analyse?",
  "faq_a3": "The AI compares each trade to your strategy described in natural language. It detects rule violations, behavioural patterns (revenge trading, FOMO, overtrading) and gives you concrete recommendations.",
  "faq_q4": "Is my data secure?",
  "faq_a4": "Yes. Your data is stored securely on Supabase (encrypted PostgreSQL infrastructure). Only you can access it. We never sell any data.",
  "faq_q5": "What's the difference between Plus and Premium?",
  "faq_a5": "The Plus plan is the daily coach: 1 AI analysis per day and the AI Coach, 5 messages per day. The Premium plan adds automation and protection: automatic account sync, challenge guardian, daily macro analysis, and wider quotas: up to 2 analyses per day within a cap of 40 per month, and up to 30 coach messages per day within a cap of 340 per month.",
  "faq_q6": "Can I cancel at any time?",
  "faq_a6": "Yes, no commitment or cancellation fees. You can cancel from your account settings at any time.",
  "faq_q7": "How do the AI quotas work?",
  "faq_a7": "There are two limits, and both apply at once: one per day and one per month. On Premium you can send up to 30 coach messages in a single day, within a cap of 340 for the month. The daily limit exists so you can run a long session when you need one; the monthly one is the overall envelope. If you used all 30 every single day, you would reach the envelope before the end of the month: we tell you plainly when that happens, and we can raise it on your account if your usage justifies it. Same principle for analyses: 2 per day, 40 per month.",
