  "coh_grav_incomplet": "A rule is missing",
  "coh_serie_depasse_dd_jour": "Your stop rule lets you string together {pertes} losses at {risque}%, that is -{perte}% of capital. Your account is disqualified at -{limite}% in a day: you are out before your own rule even fires.",
  "coh_serie_depasse_dd_total": "{pertes} losses in a row cost -{perte}% of capital, while your account stops at -{limite}% in total. One bad streak ends everything.",
  "coh_exposition_depasse_dd_jour": "{trades} trades at {risque}% in the same day expose {exposition}% of capital, against a daily limit of {limite}%. Your pace and your risk cannot coexist.",
  "coh_serie_lourde": "{pertes} losses in a row at {risque}% cost you -{perte}% of capital. That is what your own stop rule allows before pulling you out.",
  "coh_risque_par_trade": "At {risque}% per trade, it takes {pertes} losses in a row to lose half your account. You decide whether that streak looks out of reach.",
  "coh_arret_inatteignable": "You stop after {pertes} consecutive losses but you only take {trades} trades a day: this rule can never fire within a session. It reassures you without protecting you.",
  "coh_cadence_intenable": "{trades} trades in {minutes} minutes is {parTrade} minutes per trade, analysis included. Check that you can really execute at that pace without skipping a step.",
  "coh_manque_invalidation": "No invalidation point. It is the rule people forget, and the only one whose absence makes all the others uncheckable: without it you do not know you are wrong, so your loss is undefined, so your position size is too.",
